\b DKSI Revit Tools\b0\par
Internal tools for Revit 2027. For use within DKSI and by colleagues invited to evaluate them.\par
\par
\b What this installs\b0\par
A Revit add-in, into your own user profile only. It needs no administrator rights and changes no system settings. Everything lands in %AppData%\\Autodesk\\Revit\\Addins\\2027 and can be removed from Apps & features at any time.\par
\par
\b What it does to your models\b0\par
The tools read your model and, when you ask them to, write measured quantities into room and element parameters. Every write happens in a single transaction, so one Ctrl+Z undoes a whole run. Nothing is deleted or replaced: existing parameters keep their definition, their identity and their data.\par
\par
\b Logs and reports\b0\par
Runs produce a log and a CSV under %LocalAppData%\\Cda\\RevitAddin. These stay on your machine.\par
\par
\b Time tracking\b0\par
The add-in includes a time-tracking feature that records time per project and view. It is switched OFF by this installer. Nothing is recorded unless you turn it on yourself from the DKSI tab.\par
\par
\b No warranty\b0\par
These are internal tools under active development. Check quantities before they leave the office.\par
